    <div class="ed-beliefs__text">
      <div class="ed-beliefs__head">
        <span class="ed-lbl">Beliefs</span>
        <h2>What I optimize for.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="ed-beliefs__copy">
        <p>Security only works when the architecture actually survives contact with a <em>live adversary</em>. Building resilient systems means tracking behavioral tradecraft instead of just chasing indicators, treating trust as something that must be earned continuously. A network will only hold up under pressure if the environment remains <em>completely legible</em>.</p>
        <p>Ultimately, this profession is just figuring out how things break and engineering them to be much harder to crack. I have always loved that part.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ed-beliefs__imgs">
      <div class="ed-frame ed-frame--a ed-bento" role="group" aria-label="Cybersecurity snapshot: an animated dot-matrix eagle tracked by a reframing grid, live threat intelligence from OTX and CIRCL MISP, six security certifications, and a rotating MITRE ATT&amp;CK technique spotlight">
        <div class="ed-bento__cell ed-bento__pixels">
          <span class="ed-bento__lbl" title="Ambient animation, not a live readout.">Signal</span>
          <canvas id="ed-bento-pixels" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-bento__cell ed-bento__intel">
          <span class="ed-bento__lbl" title="Fresh threat reports shared by two open security-research communities, OTX and MISP."><span class="ed-intel__dot"></span>Threat intel · OTX + MISP</span>
          <div class="ed-intel__list" id="ed-intel-list"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-bento__cell ed-bento__certs">
          <span class="ed-bento__lbl" title="Six industry certifications, verified on Credly.">Certifications&#8202;·&#8202;6</span>
          <div class="ed-badges__wrap">
            <div class="ed-badges__track" id="ed-badges-track"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-bento__cell ed-bento__attck">
          <span class="ed-bento__lbl" title="Real attacker techniques from MITRE ATT&CK, the standard catalog of how intrusions happen. A new one every few seconds; click a dot to pick.">MITRE ATT&amp;CK · techniques</span>
          <div id="ed-attck-mount"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Was a static stock photo, then briefly a live Cloudflare Radar
           rotator — now a decorative autoplay runner game, security-reskinned.
           Pure attract mode: never reads input, dies and restarts forever,
           purely ambient like the nebula ships / subliminal glitch layer. AI jump
           timing uses a fixed reaction distance that doesn't scale with the
           game's own speed ramp — deliberate, so it plays cleanly at first
           and eventually mistimes a jump as it speeds up, giving each run a
           natural ~15-25s length instead of running forever or looking
           obviously scripted. -->
      <figure class="ed-frame ed-frame--b ed-arcade" aria-label="Decorative animation: an autoplaying security-themed runner game, not interactive">
        <span class="ed-bento__lbl ed-arcade__lbl" title="Decorative auto-playing animation. It plays itself and restarts forever.">Ambient · auto-playing</span>
        <canvas id="ed-arcade-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Research log -->
  <section class="ed-log" aria-label="From the research log">
    <div class="ed-log__head">
      <div>
        <span class="ed-lbl">Research log</span>
        <h2>Recent writing.</h2>
      </div>
      <a href="/blog">Read the blog →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="ed-grid">
      {recentPosts.map((p, i) => (
        <a class="ed-card" href={p.href}>
          <div class="ed-ph"><span class="ed-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><img loading="lazy" src={p.img} alt={p.title}></div>
          <div class="ed-cmeta"><span>{p.cat}</span><span>{p.date}</span></div>
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p>{p.desc}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<!-- index-editorial-flow.js is now lazy-loaded from the anchor at the top of #editorial, see above -->
<!-- ═══════════════ END EDITORIAL FLOW ═══════════════ -->

